\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Agentic post-training run}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{agent}
\tag{post-training}

\p{An \newvocab{agentic post-training run} fixes a finite round count
#{N_{\rm ag}\geq0}, an initial state #{\Sigma_0}, a fixed accounting dimension
#{m\geq1}, a componentwise budget #{b_{\rm ag}\in\mathbb R_+^m}, and the round
specifications of \ref{ftip-0073}. Put
#{\Omega_{\rm ag}=\prod_{n=0}^{N_{\rm ag}-1}\Omega_n}, using a singleton for
the empty product. Once those specifications and their exact versions
#{v_{\rm ag}} are fixed, the run is the map}

##{
\mathsf{Run}_{\Sigma_0,v_{\rm ag}}:\Omega_{\rm ag}\longrightarrow
\mathcal M_{\rm exec}\times\mathcal R_{\rm ag}^{N_{\rm ag}}
\times\mathbb R_+^m.
}

\p{Write a realized round-seed tuple as}

##{
\omega_{\rm ag}=(\omega_0,\ldots,\omega_{N_{\rm ag}-1}).
}

\p{The run recursively constructs #{\Sigma_1,\ldots,\Sigma_{N_{\rm ag}}};
the seed tuple and state sequence are empty beyond #{\Sigma_0} when
#{N_{\rm ag}=0}. Its cumulative realized cost is
##{
c_{\rm ag}=\sum_{n=0}^{N_{\rm ag}-1}c_n.
}
The empty sum is #{0\in\mathbb R_+^m} when #{N_{\rm ag}=0}.
The map returns #{(M_{N_{\rm ag}},\mathcal L_{N_{\rm ag}},c_{\rm ag})}. A run
claiming the hard budget
must declare a pre-admission or stopping rule that guarantees
#{c_{\rm ag}\preceq b_{\rm ag}}.}

\p{The run declaration includes the task sampler, environments, serializers,
rollout inference settings, feedback and credit maps, update maps, stopping
rule, seed laws, implementation versions, and resource account. The round
records retain every realized seed, version, decision, and cost. Leaving one of
these fields implicit defines a family of runs rather than one reproducible
intervention.}
